  "case": "The readers are funders, reached through Harborlight board members talking about the sixth site. They must come away believing that need is outgrowing our five sites, and that a sixth site at Eastgate would serve more adults with work that is proven. The strongest evidence: enrollment grew from 936 to 1,148, 287 adults were still waiting at year end, the average wait was nine weeks, and 68 percent of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained a reading level, at $1,237 per learner. Funders will ask what the new site adds and what it costs. The ask is help funding the $190,000 increase, from $1,420,000 in FY2026 spending to a $1,610,000 FY2027 budget, to open a sixth site at the Eastgate branch library with two site coordinators.",
